  "title": "owned, redis, aside, relaxed",
  "summary": "A shared Redis with a recorded maxmemory and allkeys-lru policy (approximate LRU, and the report says so). Cache-aside: a miss takes a per-key fill lease, double-checks, loads a committed view and publishes it. A reader may receive an older committed value than the latest acknowledged write, and every such read is counted. The owned model supplies a monotonic cache_version to fence and validate against.",
  "risk": "may return stale committed data; throughput is only reportable with the wrong-read count and rate beside it",
